{"is":"issue","title":"nginx HTTP/2 CVEs","body":"\u003cp\u003eA number of vulnerabilities have recently been disclosed in nginx (\u003ca href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-123007\"\u003eCVE-2026-123007\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-123633\"\u003eCVE-2026-123633\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-123634\"\u003eCVE-2026-123634\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-121810\"\u003eCVE-2026-121810\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-113425\"\u003eCVE-2026-113425\u003c/a\u003e), fixed upstream in nginx 1.30.7 and 1.31.9. They only affect nginx when HTTP/2 is enabled, and our configs enable HTTP/2 out of the box. Unless you have turned HTTP/2 off, for example by adding \u003ccode\u003ehttp2 off\u003c/code\u003e to a server block in SWAG or nginx, you should update.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have rebuilt every affected image whose distro has shipped a fixed package anyway. At the time of writing only \u003cstrong\u003eAlpine 3.24\u003c/strong\u003e (nginx \u003ccode\u003e1.30.7-r0\u003c/code\u003e) and \u003cstrong\u003eArch Linux\u003c/strong\u003e (nginx \u003ccode\u003e1.30.7-1\u003c/code\u003e) have published updates. Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora and Kali have not shipped a fixed nginx yet. We will rebuild the images based on them once they do, and update this post.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe images based on Selkies (webtop and our other GUI desktop apps) only use nginx internally to serve the web interface, and they never enable HTTP/2 unless you edit the nginx configuration yourself. They are not exposed in their default state, whether they have been rebuilt yet or not.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you are using pinned image tags, be aware that these patches will \u003cem\u003enot\u003c/em\u003e be backported to older image versions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe following images have been updated:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight\"\u003e\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\" style=\"color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"language-text\" data-lang=\"text\"\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eardour:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eazahar:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ebabybuddy:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ebookstack:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ecops:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003edarktable:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003edokuwiki:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003efreshrss:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003egitqlient:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003egrav:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003egrocy:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ehandbrake:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eheimdall:development\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eheimdall:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003einkscape:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eintellij-idea:latest\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"display:flex;\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e